 ## Endpoints
 
-- `GET /items` → `{"items": [...]}`: every item, ordered by `id`.
+- `GET /items?limit=<n>&cursor=<token>` →
+  `{"items": [...], "next_cursor": "..." | null}`: items ordered by `id`.
+  `limit` is an integer from 1 through 100 and defaults to 20. `cursor` is an
+  opaque token returned by the previous page; omit it on the first request.
+  `next_cursor` is null when there are no more items. Invalid limits and
+  malformed or unknown cursors return HTTP 400 with `{"error": "..."}`.
 - `GET /items/<id>` → the item, 404 when unknown, 400 when `id` is not a number.
 
 Run the tests with `python3 -m unittest`.
